<td align="left" valign="top">PolyUb,p-S166,S188-MDM2<br>Mouse double minute 2 homolog isoform MDM2; Mdm2, transformed 3T3 cell double minute 2, p53 binding protein (mouse); p53-binding protein Mdm2; oncoprotein MDM2; ubiquitin-protein ligase E3 Mdm2. Mdm2, a target of p53, interacts with a variety of proteins including Rb and E2F-1 to promote the G1-S cell cycle transition. MDM2 contains a carboxy-terminal RING finger domain, which functions as a ubiquitin E3 ligase for p53 and itself. Mdm2 is overexpressed in a variety of human cancers including 30% of sarcomas. Note that the listed GeneID refers to multiple variants encoded by the same gene. The precise molecular variant involved in this interaction is not specified.<br>Mouse double minute 2 homolog isoform MDM2. This is a modeled interaction record. Any identifier listed below refers to the molecules being modeled, not to the molecules that were actually shown to interact.<br>Mouse double minute 2 homolog isoform MDM2e<br>Ubiquitin-protein ligase E3 Mdm2 (MDM2)<br>Mouse double minute 2 homolog isoform Mdm2; Mdm2, transformed 3T3 cell double minute 2, p53 binding protein (mouse); p53-binding protein Mdm2; oncoprotein Mdm2; ubiquitin-protein ligase E3 Mdm2. Mdm2, a target of p53, interacts with a variety of proteins including Rb and E2F-1 to promote the G1-S cell cycle transition. Mdm2 contains a carboxy-terminal RING finger domain, which functions as a ubiquitin E3 ligase for p53 and itself. Mdm2 is overexpressed in a variety of human cancers including 30% of sarcomas. Note that the listed GeneID refers to multiple variants encoded by the same gene. The precise molecular variant involved in this interaction is not specified.<br>mdm2-A<br>Ubiquitin-protein ligase E3 Mdm2 (p53-binding protein Mdm2) (Oncoprotein Mdm2) (Double minute 2 protein) (Hdm2) [BLAST Evalue to experimental molecule = 1.00e-37]<br>Oncoprotein Mdm2 (mRNA)<br>Ubiquitin-protein ligase E3 Mdm2<br>p-S166,S188,T218-MDM2<br>Mdm2, transformed 3T3 cell double minute 2, p53 binding protein MDM2; mouse double minute 2 homolog isoform MDM2; oncoprotein MDM2.<br>Ub,p-MDM2<br>Ub,p-S166,S188-MDM2<br>Mouse double minute 2 homolog isoform MDM2, a nuclear phosphoprotein that binds and inhibits transactivation by tumor protein p53. This protein has E3 ubiquitin ligase activity.<br>mdm2<br>Transformed 3T3 cell double minute 2, p53 binding protein (mouse); oncoprotein Mdm2. Mdm2 functions as a regulator of p53 and has E3 ubiquitin ligase activity. Note that the listed GeneID refers to multiple variants encoded by the same gene. The precise molecular variant involved in this interaction is not specified.<br>p53-binding protein Mdm2<br>Ub,p-S166,188-MDM2<br>MDM2<br>Ubiquitin-Protein Ligase E3 Mdm2<br>mouse double minute 2 homolog isoform MDM2.<br>p-5S,T-MDM2<br>E3 ubiquitin-protein ligase Mdm2 (mRNA)<br>Mouse double minute 2 homolog isoform Mdm2; ubiquitin-protein ligase E3 Mdm2; Mdm2, transformed 3T3 cell double minute 2, p53 binding protein (mouse); p53-binding protein Mdm2; oncoprotein Mdm2. Mdm2, a target of p53, interacts with a variety of proteins including Rb and E2F-1 to promote the G1-S cell cycle transition. Mdm2 contains a carboxy-terminal RING finger domain, which functions as a ubiquitin E3 ligase for p53 and itself. Mdm2 is overexpressed in a variety of human cancers including 30% of sarcomas. Note that the listed GeneID refers to multiple variants encoded by the same gene. The precise molecular variant involved in this interaction is not specified.<br>Transformed 3T3 cell double minute 2, p53 binding protein (mouse); oncoprotein mdm2; mouse double minute 2 homolog isoform MDM2. Mdm2 functions as a regulator of p53 and has E3 ubiquitin ligase activity. Multiple isoforms arise from alternative splicing of this gene. The GI listed here represents the long isoform. This is a modeled interaction record. Any identifier listed below refers to the molecules being modeled, not to the molecules that were actually shown to interact.<br>mdm2 gene promoter. Note that the listed GI refers to Homo sapiens chromosome 12, complete sequence. The sequence [67488952-67489081], which encoded the region of the mdm2 gene promoter that was amplified and studied by the authors, was inferred from the PCR primer sequences.<br>Mdm2, transformed 3T3 cell double minute 2, p53 binding protein (mouse)<br>p-MDM2<br>Mdm2<br>MDM2_HUMAN<br>Mouse double minute 2 homolog; ubiquitin-protein ligase E3 Mdm2; Mdm2, transformed 3T3 cell double minute 2, p53 binding protein (mouse); oncoprotein Mdm2. Mdm2 contains a carboxy-terminal RING finger domain, which functions as a ubiquitin E3 ligase for p53 and itself; it interacts with a variety of proteins including Rb and E2F-1 to promote the G1-S cell cycle transition. Mdm2 is overexpressed in a variety of human cancers including 30% of sarcomas. Note that the listed GeneID refers to multiple variants encoded by the same gene. The precise molecular variant involved in this interaction is not specified.<br>Mouse double minute 2 homolog isoform Mdm2; ubiquitin-protein ligase E3 Mdm2; Mdm2, transformed 3T3 cell double minute 2, p53 binding protein (mouse); p53-binding protein Mdm2; oncoprotein Mdm2. Mdm2, a target of p53, interacts with a variety of proteins including Rb and E2F-1 to promote the G1-S cell cycle transition. Mdm2 contains a carboxy-terminal RING finger domain, which functions as a ubiquitin E3 ligase for p53 and itself. Mdm2 is overexpressed in a variety of human cancers including 30% of sarcomas. Note that the listed GeneID refers to multiple variants encoded by the same gene. The precise molecular variant involved in this interaction is not specified. Note that the listed GeneID refers to multiple variants encoded by the same gene. The precise molecular variant involved in this interaction is not specified.<br>MDM2-promoter<br>mdm2_human_probe<br>p-S166,S188,S386,S395,S407,T419-MDM2<br>PolyUb,p-MDM2<br>MDM2UAS6<br>RING-type E3 ubiquitin transferase Mdm2 (mRNA)<br>P53-binding protein Mdm2 (mRNA)<br>SUMO1-K182-MDM2<br>PolyUb-MDM2<br>p53 binding protein Mdm2<br>Transformed 3T3 cell double minute 2, p53 binding protein (mouse);oncoprotein MDM2. Hdm-2 functions as a regulator of p53 and has E3 ubiquitin ligase activity. Note that the listed GeneID refers to multiple variants encoded by the same gene. The precise molecular variant involved in this interaction is not specified.<br>MDM2 Gene<br>Human homolog of; mouse double minute 2; mouse double minute 2 homolog; mouse double minute 2, human homolog of; p53-binding protein; p53-binding protein; p53-binding protein MDM2; ubiquitin-protein ligase E3 Mdm2.<br>Double minute 2 homolog isoform MDM2<br>Mouse Double Minute 2 homolog; Transformed 3T3 cell double minute 2, p53 binding protein (mouse); ubiquitin-protein ligase E3 Mdm2. HDM2 functions as a negative regulator of p53 activity and stability mediated by HDM,s E3 ligase and transcriptional-regulation activities.<br>Mouse double minute 2 homolog isoform MDM2, a nuclear phosphoprotein that binds and inhibits transactivation by tumor protein p53. This protein has E3 ubiquitin ligase activity. This is a modeled interaction record. Any identifier listed below refers to the molecules being modeled, not to the molecules that were actually shown to interact.<br>Mouse double minute 2 homolog isoform MDM2, a nuclear phosphoprotein that binds and inhibits transactivation by tumor protein p53.<br>mdm2_human<br>Homo sapiens Mdm2; transformed 3T3 cell double minute 2; p53 binding protein (mouse) (MDM2); transcript variant MDM2. Note that the listed GI refers to an incomplete description of this interacting molecule, as this interacting molecule also contains promoter sequences upstream of the transcriptional start site.<br>E3 ubiquitin-protein ligase Mdm2<br>Double minute 2 homolog isoform MDM2a<br>Mdm2 messenger RNA (MDM2 mRNA)<br>Double minute 2 homolog isoform MDM2d<br>MDM2UAS8<br>MDM2_RNA<br>Transformed 3T3 cell double minute 2, p53 binding protein (mouse). Mdm2 functions as a regulator of p53 and has E3 ubiquitin ligase activity. Various transcript variants arise from alternative splicing. This protein represents the full length isoform. This is a modeled interaction record. Any identifier listed below refers to the molecules being modeled, not to the molecules that were actually shown to interact.<br>Mdm2, p53 E3 ubiquitin protein ligase homolog (mouse)<br>Mouse double minute 2 homolog isoform MDM2,  a nuclear phosphoprotein that binds and inhibits transactivation by tumor protein p53. This protein has E3 ubiquitin ligase activity. Note that the listed GeneID refers to multiple variants encoded by the same gene. The precise molecular variant involved in this interaction is not specified. This is a modeled interaction record. Any identifier listed below refers to the molecules being modeled, not to the molecules that were actually shown to interact.<br>SUMO1 N-glycyl-lys MDM2<br>Mdm2, transformed 3T3 cell double minute 2, p53 binding protein.  Promoter of MDM2 locus.  The listed GI refers to the entire chromosome 12 genomic sequence.  The sequence range [67488247-67520481], which encodes the Mdm2 gene, was inferred from the GI.  The sequence range of the Mdm2 promoter was not specified.<br>Transformed 3T3 cell double minute 2, p53 binding protein (mouse). Mdm2 functions as a regulator of p53 and has E3 ubiquitin ligase activity. This protein represents isoform 1 of 6. OMIM:164785<br>Mouse double minute 2 homolog isoform MDM2.<br>Mdm2, transformed 3T3 cell double minute 2, p53 binding protein (mouse). Note that the listed GeneID refers to multiple variants encoded by the same gene. The precise molecular variant involved in this interaction is not specified.<br>MDM2 protein<br>Oncoprotein Mdm2<br>Mouse double minute 2 homolog isoform MDM2a<br>RING-type E3 ubiquitin transferase Mdm2<br>Mouse Double Minute 2 homolog intronic promoter, Mdm2, transformed 3T3 cell double minute 2, p53 binding protein (mouse). Note the authors state that the intronic sequence [261-524], between the first and second exons of the human MDM2 locus on human chromosome 12, was used in this study.<br>Mouse double minute 2 homolog isoform MDM2b<br>Mouse double minute 2 homolog; ubiquitin-protein ligase E3 Mdm2; Mdm2, transformed 3T3 cell double minute 2, p53 binding protein (mouse); oncoprotein Mdm2. Mdm2 contains a carboxy-terminal RING finger domain, which functions as a ubiquitin E3 ligase for p53 and itself; it interacts with a variety of proteins including Rb and E2F-1 to promote the G1-S cell cycle transition. Mdm2 is overexpressed in a variety of human cancers including 30% of sarcomas. Note that the listed GeneID refers to multiple variants encoded by the same gene. The precise molecular variant involved in this interaction is not specified. This is a modeled interaction record. Any identifier listed below refers to the molecules being modeled, not to the molecules that were actually shown to interact.<br>Mdm2, transformed 3T3 cell double minute 2, p53 binding protein. Note that the listed GeneID refers to multiple variants encoded by the same gene. The precise molecular variant involved in this interaction is not specified.<br>Phospho-MDM2<br>Transformed 3T3 cell double minute 2, p53 binding protein (mouse). Mdm2 functions as a regulator of p53 and has E3 ubiquitin ligase activity. This protein represents isoform 1 of 6.<br>Mouse double minute 2 homolog; human homolog of, p53-binding protein; mouse double minute 2; p53-binding protein MDM2; ubiquitin-protein ligase E3 Mdm2; mouse double minute 2, human homolog of, p53-binding protein. This is a modeled interaction record. Any identifier listed below refers to the molecules being modeled, not to the molecules that were actually shown to interact. Note that the listed GeneID refers to multiple variants encoded by the same gene. The precise molecular variant involved in this interaction is not specified.<br>Ubiquitin-protein ligase E3 Mdm2 (EC 6.3.2.-) (p53-binding protein Mdm2) (Oncoprotein Mdm2) (Double minute 2 protein) (Hdm2)<br>Mouse double minute 2 homolog isoform MDM2c<br>mdm2 promoter<br>Mouse double minute 2 homolog isoform MDM2,  a nuclear phosphoprotein that binds and inhibits transactivation by tumor protein p53. This protein has E3 ubiquitin ligase activity.<br>Mouse double minute 2 homolog isoform MDM2d<br>MDM2 protein (mRNA)<br>Mouse double minute 2 homolog isoform MDM2; Mdm2, transformed 3T3 cell double minute 2, p53 binding protein (mouse); p53-binding protein MDM2; oncoprotein MDM2. MDM2, a target of p53, interacts with a variety of proteins including Rb and E2F-1 to promote the G1-S cell cycle transition. MDM2 contains a carboxy-terminal RING finger domain, which functions as a ubiquitin E3 ligase for p53 and itself. MDM2 is overexpressed in a variety of human cancers including 30% of sarcomas.<br>E3 ubiquitin-protein ligase Mdm2 ecNumber6.3.2.-/ecNumber<br>Mdm2, transformed 3T3 cell double minute 2, p53 binding protein<br>MDM2_inactive<br>Promoter region of hdm2 gene. Mdm2, transformed 3T3 cell double minute 2. This p53 binding protein is a nuclear phosphoprotein which has an E3 ubiquitin ligase activity.<br>Double minute 2 homolog isoform MDM2e<br>Ubiquitin protein ligase E3 Mdm2<br>Double minute 2 homolog isoform MDM2b<br>Mouse double minute 2 homolog; ubiquitin-protein ligase E3 Mdm2; Mdm2, transformed 3T3 cell double minute 2, p53 binding protein (mouse); oncoprotein Mdm2. Mdm2 contains a carboxy-terminal RING finger domain, which functions as a ubiquitin E3 ligase for p53 and itself; it interacts with a variety of proteins including Rb and E2F-1 to promote the G1-S cell cycle transition. Mdm2 is overexpressed in a variety of human cancers including 30% of sarcomas. Note that the listed GeneID refers to multiple variants encoded by the same gene. The precise molecular variant involved in this interaction is not specified. This is a modelled interaction record. Any identifier listed below refers to the molecules being modelled, and not to the molecules that were actualy shown to interact.<br>p-S166,S188-MDM2<br>Transformed 3T3 cell double minute 2, p53 binding protein (mouse); oncoprotein mdm2; mouse double minute 2 homolog isoform MDM2. Mdm2 functions as a regulator of p53 and has E3 ubiquitin ligase activity. Multiple isoforms arise from alternative splicing of this gene. The GI listed here represents the long isoform.This is a modeled interaction record. Any identifier listed below refers to the molecules being modeled, not to the molecules that were actually shown to interact.<br>Mouse double minute 2 homolog isoform MDM2<br>MDM2 intronic promoter<br>P53-binding protein Mdm2<br>PolyUb,p-S166,188-MDM2<br>Transformed 3T3 cell double minute 2, p53 binding protein (mouse). Mdm2 functions as a regulator of p53 and has E3 ubiquitin ligase activity. Various transcript variants arise from alternative splicing. This protein represents the full length isoform.<br>p-S166,188-MDM2</td>
