</td>
<td align="left" valign="top">mdm2 promoter<br>MDM2 intronic promoter<br>mdm2_human_gene<br>MDM2 gene<br>Promoter region of hdm2 gene. Mdm2, transformed 3T3 cell double minute 2. This p53 binding protein is a nuclear phosphoprotein which has an E3 ubiquitin ligase activity.<br>Mouse Double Minute 2 homolog intronic promoter, Mdm2, transformed 3T3 cell double minute 2, p53 binding protein (mouse). Note the authors state that the intronic sequence [261-524], between the first and second exons of the human MDM2 locus on human chromosome 12, was used in this study.<br>Human MDM2 gene<br>Mdm2, transformed 3T3 cell double minute 2, p53 binding protein.  Promoter of MDM2 locus.  The listed GI refers to the entire chromosome 12 genomic sequence.  The sequence range [67488247-67520481], which encodes the Mdm2 gene, was inferred from the GI.  The sequence range of the Mdm2 promoter was not specified.<br>Homo sapiens Mdm2; transformed 3T3 cell double minute 2; p53 binding protein (mouse) (MDM2); transcript variant MDM2. Note that the listed GI refers to an incomplete description of this interacting molecule, as this interacting molecule also contains promoter sequences upstream of the transcriptional start site.<br>MDM2UAS8<br>MDM2-promoter<br>MDM2UAS6<br>MDM2_DNA<br>mdm2 gene promoter. Note that the listed GI refers to Homo sapiens chromosome 12, complete sequence. The sequence [67488952-67489081], which encoded the region of the mdm2 gene promoter that was amplified and studied by the authors, was inferred from the PCR primer sequences.<br>MDM2</td>
<td align="left" valign="top">gene</td>
