<td align="left" valign="top">Reprimo, TP53 dependant G2 arrest mediator candidate. Note that the listed GI refers to the entire chromosome 2 genomic sequence. The sequence range [154160330-154161830], which encoded the region of REPRIMO promoter that was amplified and studied by the authors, is the sequence [-1000 - +500] relative to the transcription start site as mapped to the GI.</td>
<td align="left" valign="top">rna</td>
<td align="left" valign="top"><b><a href="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/Tools/webservices/psicquic/view/main.xhtml?conversationContext=1" target="_blank" title="Bind" style="color:#ffdbab;">B</a> <a href="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/Tools/webservices/psicquic/view/main.xhtml?conversationContext=1" target="_blank" title="Bind" style="color:#ffdbab;">B</a> <a href="http://www.thebiogrid.org/SearchResults/summary/121145" target="_blank" title="Biogrid" style="color:#55ff55;">B</a> <a href="http://www.hprd.org/summary?hprd_id=18002&isoform_id=18002_1&isoform_name" target="_blank" title="Hprd" style="color:#aa5500;">H</a></b></td>
</tr>
<tr bgcolor="#E1FFE1">
<td valign="top" align="center">
<input type="checkbox" name="objs:list" value="139005">
</td>
<td align="left" valign="top">Arylalkylamine N-acetyltransferase belongs to the superfamily of acetyltransferases. It is the penultimate enzyme in melatonin synthesis and controls the night/day rhythm in melatonin production in the vertebrate pineal gland. Melatonin is essential for seasonal reproduction, modulates the function of the circadian clock in the suprachiasmatic nucleus, and influences activity and sleep. This enzyme is rapidly inactivated when animals are exposed to light at night. This protein is 80% identical to sheep and rat AA-NAT. Arylalkylamine N-acetyltransferase may contribute a multifactorial genetic diseases such as altered behavior in sleep/wake cycle. [BLAST Evalue to experimental molecule = 1.16e-87]</td>
<td align="left" valign="top">protein</td>
<td align="left" valign="top"><b><a href="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/Tools/webservices/psicquic/view/main.xhtml?conversationContext=1" target="_blank" title="Bind" style="color:#ffdbab;">B</a> <a href="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/Tools/webservices/psicquic/view/main.xhtml?conversationContext=1" target="_blank" title="Bind" style="color:#ffdbab;">B</a> <a href="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/Tools/webservices/psicquic/view/main.xhtml?conversationContext=1" target="_blank" title="Bind" style="color:#ffdbab;">B</a> <a href="http://www.thebiogrid.org/SearchResults/summary/106533" target="_blank" title="Biogrid" style="color:#55ff55;">B</a> <a href="http://www.hprd.org/summary?hprd_id=02974&isoform_id=02974_1&isoform_name" target="_blank" title="Hprd" style="color:#aa5500;">H</a> <a href="http://biocyc.org/HUMAN/NEW-IMAGE?type=NIL&object=HS05303-MONOMER" target="_blank" title="Humancyc" style="color:#aa00aa;">H</a> <a href="http://www.innatedb.ca/advancedSearch.do?taxonID=all&field1=idphysical_molecule&keyword1=69711&operator1=AND&field2=&keyword2=&operator2=AND&field3=&keyword3=&operator3=AND&field4=&keyword4=&listType=gene" target="_blank" title="Innatedb" style="color:#ffcc88;">I</a> <a href="http://www.inoh.org/" target="_blank" title="Inoh" style="color:#ffb7b7;">I</a> <a href="http://www.inoh.org/" target="_blank" title="Inoh" style="color:#ffb7b7;">I</a> <a href="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/intact/search/do/search?searchString=MINT-1559914" target="_blank" title="Intact" style="color:#00aaaa;">I</a> <a href="http://www.ebi.ac.uk/intact/search/do/search?searchString=EBI-7451846" target="_blank" title="Intact" style="color:#00aaaa;">I</a> <a href="http://www.genome.jp/dbget-bin/www_bget?hsa:15" target="_blank" title="Kegg" style="color:#00aa00;">K</a> <a href="https://mint.bio.uniroma2.it/index.php/results-interactions/?id=Q16613" target="_blank" title="Mint" style="color:#55ffff;">M</a> <a href="http://molvis.vbi.vt.edu/pig/view/pig_protein_view.php?protein=SNAT_HUMAN" target="_blank" title="Pi